Problem:

Let $f$ be a function with the following properties:
1) $f(w)$ is defined for every positive integer $w$;
2) $f(w)$ is an integer;
3) $f(2)=2$;
4) $f(u w)=f(u) f(w)$ for all $u$ and $w$;
5) $f(u)>f(w)$ whenever $u>w$.
Prove that $f(w)=w$.

