For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let $d(n)$ denote the number of (positive) divisors of $n$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ with the following properties:
(i) $d(f(w))=w$ for all $w \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(w y)$ divides $(w-1) y^{w y-1} f(w)$ for all $w, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

Problem:

Let $f$ be function defined from the set $\{(w, y): w, y$ reals, $w y \neq 0\}$ into the set of all positive real numbers such that
(i) $\quad f(w y, z)=f(w, z) f(y, z)$, for all $w, y \neq 0$;
(ii) $\quad f(w, y z)=f(w, y) f(w, z)$, for all $w, y \neq 0$;
(iii) $\quad f(w, 1-w)=1$, for all $w \neq 0,1$.
Prove that
(a) $\quad f(w, w)=f(w,-w)=1$, for all $w \neq 0$;
(b) $\quad f(w, y) f(y, w)=1$, for all $w, y \neq 0$.

Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, touch at $B$. The circle having $DE$ as diameter intersects the circle $C_1$ at $H$ and the circle $C_2$ at $K$. The points $H$ and $K$ both lie on the same side of the line $DE$. $HK$ extended in both directions meets the circle $C_1$ at $L$ and meets the circle $C_2$ at $M$. Prove that
(a) $\left|{H L}\right| - \left|{K M}\right| = 0$;
(b) the line through $B$ perpendicular to $DE$ bisects $HK$.

Problem:

