Given an integer $n - 3 \geq 0$. Consider $n$ real numbers $x_1, x_2, \dots, x_n$ satisfying at the same time the following conditions:

i/  $x_1 \ge x_2 \ge \dots \ge x_n$;
ii/  $\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = 0$;
iii/  $\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i^2 = n(n-1)$.

Find the maximum and the minimum values of the sum $S = x_1 + x_2$.

